<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Nightingale is a 38-year-old woman with post-infectious ME/CFS, managed with energy management since March, and a past brucellosis treated abroad, who asked for a same-day visit. Three days ago she developed a sore throat and runny nose, followed by a dry cough. A colleague who visited to work with her had a cold last week. Two home COVID-19 antigen tests, two days apart, were negative. Her highest home temperature was 37.8 °C. Since yesterday her fatigue, muscle aches, and brain fog have been much worse than her usual day-to-day variation, and she has spent most of both days in bed. She has already started her written flare plan: she cancelled her meetings, cut her work to short reading periods, and is resting in a darkened room. She is drinking about 2 L a day and taking acetaminophen 1 g twice a day, which helps the sore throat and aches. She has no night sweats, back or joint pain, or other symptoms resembling those of her illness abroad, and she wanted to be sure this is not that infection returning. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Three days ago, after a visitor with a cold</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Throat, nose, and chest; generalized muscle aches</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>Three days</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Dry cough, clear nasal discharge, scratchy throat</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Moderate; ME/CFS symptoms flared beyond her usual variation, mostly in bed for two days</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>Cough worse at night; fatigue worse since yesterday</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Close contact with a cold; two negative home COVID-19 antigen tests</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Acetaminophen, fluids, and rest help; flare plan started</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Low-grade temperature to 37.8 °C. Denies night sweats, back or joint pain, chest pain, breathlessness, ear or sinus pain, and sputum</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Constitutional</td><td>Positive</td><td>Marked fatigue beyond her baseline; temperature to 37.8 °C; no chills, rigors, night sweats, or weight loss</td></tr><tr><td>Ears, nose, mouth, and throat</td><td>Positive</td><td>Sore throat, clear rhinorrhea, and congestion; no ear pain or facial pain</td></tr><tr><td>Respiratory</td><td>Positive</td><td>Dry cough; no wheeze, sputum, or breathlessness</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiovascular</td><td>Positive</td><td>More lightheaded on standing than usual; no chest pain or syncope</td></tr><tr><td>Musculoskeletal</td><td>Positive</td><td>Generalized muscle aches; no localized back, hip, or joint pain or swelling</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>Positive</td><td>Brain fog worse than usual; no headache beyond mild sinus pressure; no neck stiffness</td></tr><tr><td>Gastrointestinal</td><td>Negative</td><td>No nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, or abdominal pain; eating small meals</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>7 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

